<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Diu (1509)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1509">1509</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Diu · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-mamluk-naval-war">Portuguese–Mamluk naval war</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Diu was a naval battle fought in 1509 off Diu on the west coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. A Portuguese fleet under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-de-almeida">Francisco de Almeida</a> defeated a combined fleet of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluk Sultanate</a>, the Sultanate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zamorin">Zamorin</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calicut">Calicut</a>. The victory established Portuguese naval dominance in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabian-sea">Arabian Sea</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-diu-1509.jpg" alt="Battle of Diu (1509)" width="320" height="237" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Maurício José do Carmo Sendim (1786-1870) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Insigne_vit%C3%B3ria_alcan%C3%A7ada_pelo_Vice-Rei_D._Francisco_de_Almeida_contra_as_armadas_do_Sult%C3%A3o_do_Egito,_e_dos_Reis_de_Cambaia_e_Calecute.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
